{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>a quiet man</b> — ס\"ת שם (an acrostic of שם): he dwelt in the tents of Shem to learn. ת\"ם שנים — [he dwelt] two years from when they entered the Land until the House was built; a hint to 'after ת\"ם שנים (two years complete) he dwells in tents of the Shekhinah.'" "<b>dwelling in tents</b> — עולה ת\"י (gematria 416), for thus the Shekhinah dwelt in a tent. יעקב — in gematria מלאך האלהים, and in gematria הגן עדן, and in gematria וירחך לא יאסף."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {0 "The notarikon ת\"ם שנים reads as 'two years complete' (תמימים שנים), likely alluding to Genesis 11:23 or similar chronological tradition; the bracketed יושב appears in the source and is rendered as supplied.", 1 "עולה ת\"י: the letters ת and י (400+10+6=416) match the gematria of יושב אוהלים. The last equated phrase וירחך לא יאסף is textually uncertain; rendered hyper-literally as written."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:17:01.485793947Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}